 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "In the following questions, assume there is a constant ratio between units of A and units of B. Two students are having a discussion. Determine who is correct: Student 1, Student 2, both, or neither.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 544704,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Student 1 says that the number of units of A is the product of the number of units of B times the ratio of A to B.<br>\nStudent 2 says that the number of units of A is the quotient of the number of units of B divided by the ratio of A to B.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Student 1:</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"A = B \\cdot \\frac{A}{B}\"></span></td>\n<td>This is true because the right side simplifies to A.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Student 2:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = B \\div \\frac{A}{B}\"></span></p>\n<p>This is the same as</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"A = B \\cdot \\frac{B}{A}\"></span></td>\n<td>This is not true because the left side does not equal the right side.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Student 1 is correct.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Student 1 is correct."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 544705,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Student 1 says that the number of units of A is the quotient of the number of units of B divided by the ratio of B to A.<br>\nStudent 2 says that the number of units of B is the quotient of the number of units of A divided by the ratio of A to B.\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Student 1:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = B \\div \\frac{B}{A}\"></span></p>\n<p>This is the same as</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"A = B \\cdot \\frac{A}{B}\"></span></td>\n<td>This is true because the right side simplifies to A.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Student 2:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"B = A \\div \\frac{A}{B}\"></span></p>\n<p>This is the same as</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"B = A \\cdot \\frac{B}{A}\"></span></td>\n<td>This is true because the right side simplifies to B.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Both students are correct.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Both are correct."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 544706,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Suppose there are 110 of item A and 55 of item B.<br>\nStudent 1 says the ratio of A to B is <span data-math=\"\\frac{1}{2}\">\\frac{1}{2} .</span> Student 2 says the ratio of B to A is <span data-math=\"\\frac{1}{0.5}\">\\frac{1}{0.5}\"&gt;.</span> .\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Student 1:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{A}{B} = \\frac{{110}}{{55}} = 2\"></span></p>\n<p>Student 1 is wrong.</p>\n<p>Student 2:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{B}{A} = \\frac{{55}}{{110}} = \\frac{1}{2}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{1}{{0.5}} = 2\"></span></p>\n<p>Student 2 is wrong.</p>\n<p>Both students are incorrect.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Neither are correct."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 544707,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Suppose the constant ratio of A to B is 0.75. Student 1 says the ratio of A to B is <span data-math=\"\\frac{4}{3}\">\\frac{4}{3}</span> \nStudent 2 says the ratio of B to A is <span data-math=\"\\frac{3}{4}\">\\frac{3}{4}</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Given: <span data-math=\"\\frac{A}{B} = 0.75\"></span></p>\n<p>Student 1:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{A}{B} = \\frac{4}{3} \\approx 1.3333\"></span></p>\n<p>Student 1 is wrong.</p>\n<p>Student 2:</p>\n<p>B to A should be <span data-math=\"\\frac{1}{{0.75}} \\approx 1.33333\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Student 2 says B to A is <span data-math=\"\\frac{3}{4} = 0.75\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Student 2 is wrong.</p>\n<p>Both students are wrong.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Neither are correct."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 544708,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Student 1 says that <span data-math=\"{\\text{Standard Divisor}} = \\frac{{{\\text{House Size}}}}{{{\\text{Total Population}}}}\">{\\text{Standard Divisor}} = \\frac{{{\\text{House Size}}}}{{{\\text{Total Population}}}}</span>. Student 2 says that <span data-math=\"{\\text{Standard Divisor}} = \\frac{{{\\text{Sum of the State Populations}}}}{{{\\text{Total Number of Seats Available}}}}\"></span> .",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Student 1 is incorrect. <span data-math=\"{\\text{Standard Divisor = }}\\frac{{{\\text{Total Population}}}}{{{\\text{House Size}}}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Student 2 is correct. <span data-math=\"{\\text{Standard Divisor = }}\\frac{{{\\text{Total Population}}}}{{{\\text{House Size}}}}\"></span>. The total population is the sum of the state populations. The house size is the total number of seats available.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Student 2 is correct."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 544709,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Student 1 says that <span data-math=\"{\\text{State's Standard Divisor}} = \\frac{{{\\text{Total Population}}}}{{{\\text{State's Standard Quota}}}}\">{\\text{State's Standard Divisor}} = \\frac{{{\\text{Total Population}}}}{{{\\text{State's Standard Quota}}}}</span>.\n<br>Student 2 says that <span data-math=\"{\\text{State's Standard Quota}} = \\frac{{{\\text{State Population}}}}{{{\\text{Standard Divisor}}}}\"></span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Student 1 is incorrect. The House Size should be in the denominator. <span data-math=\"{\\text{Standard Divisor = }}\\frac{{{\\text{Total Population}}}}{{{\\text{House Size}}}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Student 2 is correct. <span data-math=\"{\\text{Standard Quota = }}\\frac{{{\\text{State Population}}}}{{{\\text{Standard Divisor}}}}\"></span></p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Student 2 is correct."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 544710,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Student 1 says that <span data-math=\"{\\text{State's Standard Quota}} = {\\text{State Population }} \\div \\frac{{{\\text{Total Population}}}}{{{\\text{House Size}}}}\">{\\text{State's Standard Quota}} = {\\text{State Population }} \\div \\frac{{{\\text{Total Population}}}}{{{\\text{House Size}}}}</span>.\n<br>Student 2 says that <span data-math=\"{\\text{State's Standard Quota  = }}\\frac{{{\\text{State Population}}}}{{{\\text{Standard}}\\,{\\text{Divisor}}}}\">{\\text{State's Standard Quota  = }}\\frac{{{\\text{State Population}}}}{{{\\text{Standard}}\\,{\\text{Divisor}}}}</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Because the Standard Quota = <span data-math=\"\\frac{{{\\text{State Population}}}}{{{\\text{Standard Divisor}}}}{\\text{ seats }}\"></span> and the <span data-math=\"{\\text{Standard Divisor = }}\\frac{{{\\text{Total Population}}}}{{{\\text{House Size}}}}\"></span>,</p>\n<p>both students are correct. Student 1 substituted the Standard Divisor expression into the Standard Quota formula.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Both are correct."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
